    "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::generate_image_cross_pack_hub": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::generate_image_cross_pack_hub",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "generate_image.run is a cross-pack hub: 7+ sibling packs import its private helpers, breaking pack-as-boundary",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/packs/builtin/generate_image/run.py",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/vary_grid/run.py",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/animate_image/run.py",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/logo_ideas/run.py",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/transcribe/run.py",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/visual_understand/run.py",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/sprite_sheet/run.py",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/audio_understand/run.py",
          "astrid/packs/external/fal_foley/run.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "vary_grid/run.py:17, animate_image/run.py:19, logo_ideas/run.py:18, transcribe/run.py:14 all `from astrid.packs.builtin.generate_image.run import _candidate_env_files, _read_env_value` \u2014 six call sites importing the same two underscore-prefixed (i.e. module-private) helpers across pack boundaries.",
          "fal_foley/run.py:19 reaches further to `from astrid.packs.builtin.vary_grid.run import _load_env_var`, chaining the private dependency through a second pack.",
          "visual_understand/run.py:19, audio_understand/run.py:18, sprite_sheet/run.py:22 also import from generate_image.run (load_api_key and others), making generate_image a de-facto shared library disguised as a sibling pack.",
          "Pack boundaries in this repo are intended to be discrete (each pack has its own pack.yaml/run.py and is discovered by registry.discover_packs); a hidden mesh of cross-pack imports on private symbols means a refactor inside generate_image.run silently ripples to 7+ packs."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Extract the env-file/env-var helpers (and load_api_key) into a shared, public module under astrid/packs/_core/ (e.g. astrid/packs/_core/env_keys.py) and have generate_image and the other packs all import from there with non-underscore names. This converts a cross-pack hub through private symbols into a true shared utility with one obvious owner and removes the need for sibling packs to know about each other.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "0f583864"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
      "issue_kind": "review_defect",
      "origin": "review_import",
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::core_private_cross_module_imports": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::core_private_cross_module_imports",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Three core modules import underscore-prefixed (module-private) names across package boundaries",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/runner.py",
          "astrid/core/executor/runner.py",
          "astrid/core/timeline/cli.py",
          "astrid/core/task/run_audit.py",
          "astrid/orchestrate/dsl.py",
          "astrid/core/task/plan.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/core/orchestrator/runner.py:15 \u2014 `from astrid.core.executor.runner import _has_value, _stringify_value`. The orchestrator package is conceptually a peer of executor; reaching into executor's private names couples them more tightly than the public API admits.",
          "astrid/core/timeline/cli.py:23 \u2014 `from astrid.core.task.run_audit import _cost_by_source, _run_status`. The timeline CLI takes a private dependency on task internals.",
          "astrid/orchestrate/dsl.py:25 \u2014 `from astrid.core.task.plan import _strip_astrid_prefix`. The DSL package depends on a private helper of core.task.plan.",
          "Underscore-prefixed names in Python signal `module-private`; consuming them from a different package leaves the producer unable to refactor safely and defeats the package boundary."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Promote the three helpers to public names (drop the leading underscore and add to the module's intended public API) in their owning modules \u2014 `has_value`/`stringify_value` in astrid.core.executor.runner, `cost_by_source`/`run_status` in astrid.core.task.run_audit, `strip_astrid_prefix` in astrid.core.task.plan \u2014 and update the three importers. If a helper isn't truly suitable for public consumption, move the shared logic into a small shared module (e.g. astrid.core.executor.values, astrid.core.task.audit_view) and have both producer and consumer depend on it.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "165d7922"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
      "issue_kind": "review_defect",
      "origin": "review_import",
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
