          "cli.py line 35: `registry = load_default_registry(banodoco_config=_banodoco_config_from_args(args))`, where `_banodoco_config_from_args` (line 157+) constructs a fully-formed `BanodocoCatalogConfig` from CLI flags and env. The seam is wired on the call side and dropped on the receiver side, so `--banodoco-agent-orchestrators`, `--banodoco-catalog-url`, etc., are silently no-ops."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either (a) implement Banodoco catalog loading in the orchestrator registry the same way `load_pack_executors` + `load_banodoco_catalog_executors` is composed in the executor registry, then call it when `banodoco_config.enabled`; or (b) remove the parameter and the CLI flags entirely with a clear error if a user passes them. Do not leave a typed parameter that does nothing.",
