          "astrid/core/worker/banodoco_worker.py:228-231: `if claim is None: time.sleep(self.config.idle_sleep_sec); continue` \u2014 the long-poll loop cannot distinguish 'no work' from 'wrong service-role key' and will sleep indefinitely.",
          "Inconsistent within the same module: update_task_status (lines 184-187) raises TaskClientError on http_status >= 400, while claim_next_task does not."
        ],
        "suggestion": "In `claim_next_task`, treat HTTP 401/403 (and ideally any 4xx other than 204) as a TaskClientError so banodoco_worker.run() either crashes loudly or surfaces the failure into a structured health signal. At minimum, log at ERROR (not WARNING) for 4xx/5xx responses and increment a failure counter the worker can react to instead of silently sleeping.",
