          "astrid/contracts/schema.py:9-12 declares PORT_REQUIRED_TYPES, OUTPUT_MODES, CACHE_MODES, ISOLATION_MODES as `set[str]` allowlists that the validators then enforce, but Port.type (line 18), Output.type/mode (lines 28-29), CachePolicy.mode (line 49), and IsolationMetadata.mode (line 57) are all typed plain `str`.",
          "astrid/core/executor/schema.py:25-28 defines EXECUTOR_KINDS, EXTERNAL_RUNTIME_MODES, EXTERNAL_RUNTIME_SOURCE_KINDS, EXTERNAL_RUNTIME_INSTALL_STRATEGIES as `set[str]`; the matching dataclass fields ExecutorDefinition.kind (line 132), ExternalRuntimeSource.kind (line 106), ExternalRuntimeInstall.strategy (line 115), ExternalRuntimeMetadata.mode (line 121) are all `str` and `_validate_executor` enforces membership at runtime (lines 385-386, 517-518, 538-539, 559-560).",
          "astrid/core/reigh/task_client.py:36 declares ALLOWED_STATUSES = frozenset({\"Queued\",\"In Progress\",\"Complete\",\"Failed\",\"Cancelled\"}) and update_task_status(status: str) (line 148) checks `if status not in ALLOWED_STATUSES`. The static type promises a wider domain than the runtime accepts, and the `# type: ignore[arg-type]` it forces in astrid/core/element/registry.py:73 (`kind=kind, # type: ignore[arg-type]`) is a downstream symptom of the same thing."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Convert the string-set constants to Literal aliases co-located with the constant: e.g. in contracts/schema.py replace `OUTPUT_MODES = {\"mutate\", \"create\", \"create_or_replace\"}` with `OutputMode = Literal[\"mutate\", \"create\", \"create_or_replace\"]; OUTPUT_MODES: frozenset[OutputMode] = frozenset(get_args(OutputMode))`, then retype the corresponding fields (`mode: OutputMode = \"create_or_replace\"`). Do the same in executor/schema.py for ExecutorKind / ExternalRuntimeMode / ExternalRuntimeSourceKind / ExternalRuntimeInstallStrategy and in task_client.py for `TaskStatus`. Existing runtime checks stay as defense for untrusted JSON input but the in-process callers get correct narrowing for free.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "8ba9c1d3"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
