    "review::.::holistic::type_safety::pipeline_mode_type_ignore_arg_type": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::type_safety::pipeline_mode_type_ignore_arg_type",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "pipeline.py runpod sweep `mode: str` is silenced with `# type: ignore[arg-type]` instead of being narrowed to the Literal the callee expects",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/pipeline.py",
          "astrid/core/runpod/sweeper.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/pipeline.py:486 declares `mode: str = \"default\"`, then sets it to `\"hard\"` based on a CLI flag (line 492), and finally calls `summary = run_sweep(projects_root, mode=mode, dry_run=dry_run)  # type: ignore[arg-type]` (line 508).",
          "astrid/core/runpod/sweeper.py:110-112 declares `def sweep(... , mode: Literal[\"default\", \"hard\"] = \"default\", ...)` \u2014 the called signature already encodes the exact valid set, so the ignore is hiding the fact that the local was over-typed.",
          "Only two values are ever assigned to `mode` (\"default\" and \"hard\"); the type widening to `str` is purely for the variable declaration and serves no runtime purpose."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Type the local as the Literal directly: `mode: Literal[\"default\", \"hard\"] = \"default\"` and then `mode = \"hard\"` on the flag branch (mypy/pyright will accept both string literals as the Literal). Remove the `# type: ignore[arg-type]`. Even simpler: import the Literal alias from sweeper if you expose one (see the companion finding on string-set constants).",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "de85addd"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
      "issue_kind": "review_defect",
      "origin": "review_import",
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::type_safety::element_kinds_constant_triplicated": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::type_safety::element_kinds_constant_triplicated",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "ELEMENT_KINDS tuple defined in three modules in parallel to the ElementKind Literal \u2014 single source of truth violated for an enum-like type",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/core/element/schema.py",
          "astrid/core/pack.py",
          "astrid/structure.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/core/element/schema.py:11-12 declares `ELEMENT_KINDS = (\"effects\", \"animations\", \"transitions\")` and `ElementKind = Literal[\"effects\", \"animations\", \"transitions\"]` \u2014 the canonical pair.",
          "astrid/core/pack.py:14 redeclares `ELEMENT_KINDS = (\"effects\", \"animations\", \"transitions\")` and uses it for the same allowlist check (lines 134-138).",
          "astrid/structure.py:158 redeclares `_ELEMENT_KINDS = (\"effects\", \"animations\", \"transitions\")` for the same purpose (line 172-174).",
          "Three definitions of the same value list means the Literal type and the runtime checks can drift independently; a fourth value added in element/schema.py would silently be rejected by pack.py and structure.py."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Have astrid/core/pack.py and astrid/structure.py import `ELEMENT_KINDS` (or `tuple(get_args(ElementKind))`) from astrid/core/element/schema.py instead of redeclaring the literal tuple. One source of truth tied to the Literal alias.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "d26a52e5"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "review_defect",
      "issue_kind": "review_defect",
      "origin": "review_import",
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::type_safety::tsx_element_props_typed_any": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::type_safety::tsx_element_props_typed_any",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Pack TSX components type clip/params props as `any` while the same files type theme as `unknown` and a TimelineClip TypedDict already exists",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/text-card/component.tsx",
          "astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/neon-orbit-card/component.tsx",
          "astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/model-trends/component.tsx",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/html_canvas_effect/templates/card/component.tsx"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/text-card/component.tsx:243-256 \u2014 `props: { clip: any; params: any; theme: unknown; ... }` then immediately `const clip: any = props.clip` and casts `(clip.text ?? props.params ?? {}) as TextData`. Theme is `unknown` (correctly forces a guard) but clip and params are `any`, defeating type checking on every downstream `clip.*` access.",
          "astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/neon-orbit-card/component.tsx:68 \u2014 same `clip: any` prop typing.",
          "astrid/packs/local/elements/effects/model-trends/component.tsx:420-428 \u2014 same, plus `params: any` and another `const clip: any = props.clip`.",
          "astrid/packs/builtin/html_canvas_effect/templates/card/component.tsx:68 \u2014 same `clip: any`.",
          "astrid/timeline.py defines a precise `TimelineClip` TypedDict (and per-effect ClipEntrance/Exit/Continuous shapes) \u2014 the JSON shape these TSX components consume is already modeled on the Python side, so the pattern is not 'we don't know the shape' but 'we don't bother encoding it on the TS side'."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Replace `clip: any; params: any` with `clip: unknown; params: unknown` (mirroring the existing `theme: unknown` discipline) and force the per-component reader to narrow with a small `asTextCardClip(value: unknown): TextCardClip` guard, or generate a TS interface from the TimelineClip TypedDict and import it. Either way, eliminate the open `any` props on element components; they are a stable, copy-pasted pattern and the right place to fix once.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "9ba6dc25"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-05-15T23:50:07+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
